# 🌐 Networking Theory

# DHCP

DHCP (Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol) automatically assigns network configuration to client devices.

DHCP provides:

- IP Address
- Subnet Mask
- Default Gateway
- DNS Server

Advantages:

- Automatic configuration
- Easy management
- Reduces manual errors

---

# Static IP

A Static IP address is manually configured.

Administrator manually enters:

- IP Address
- Subnet Mask
- Default Gateway
- DNS Server

Advantages:

- Permanent address
- Reliable for servers
- Suitable for printers
- Suitable for network devices

---

# DHCP vs Static IP

| DHCP | Static IP |
|------|-----------|
| Automatic | Manual |
| IP may change | Permanent |
| Best for user computers | Best for servers and printers |
| Easy management | Requires manual configuration |

