# Key Takeaways

- Windows Services run in the background and support operating system functions.
- Print Spooler manages all print jobs.
- DHCP Client automatically receives network configuration.
- DNS Client resolves domain names into IP addresses.
- `systemctl status` checks the current status of a service.
- `journalctl -u ssh` helps identify the cause of SSH-related issues by reviewing service logs.
- DHCP is preferred for end-user devices, while Static IP is commonly used for servers and printers.

